# UI-STATUS-1 B: the status bar shows the island under the cursor, as the original (docs/re/ui.md
# 5.6; the owner chose the original, OQ-703). The developer is player 1, its city 1:1 owns all of
# island 1 (NORD, 1048..1303 x 440..695; a fixed map's developer start claims the whole
# rectangle); island 0 (NORD) holds player 0's city 0:0, which does not know player 1; island 10
# (DSCHUNGEL) has no city and nobody has discovered it; (1000, 320) is open sea.
# Facts: hud.counters (gold | residents | materials+residents), hud.status.island (slot | sea),
# hud.status.city (island:city | none), hud.fertility (segments | hidden), hud.fertility.pending
# (yes while the row's 2 s hide is pending).
# Not on lan5, covered by status_bar_test.cpp: own island outside the territory, a foreign city
# that knows the player, two own cities on one island, an armed building's corners.
# Launch: --play data/maps/lan5.txt --construction-menu on --layout data/ui
resize 1024 768
wait frames 10
# No map tile yet: gold only, the row hidden.
expect fact hud.status.tile == none
expect fact hud.counters == gold
expect fact hud.gold != none
expect fact hud.fertility == hidden
# 1. The own territory: materials, residents and the NORD row (6, 8, 11).
look 1140 516
wait frames 5
hover-land 1130 516
wait frames 5
expect fact hud.status.island == 1
expect fact hud.status.city == 1:1
expect fact hud.counters == materials+residents
expect fact hud.counters.city == 1:1
expect fact hud.fertility == 6,8,11
# 2. The pointer on the right panel: the last map tile is kept (OQ-700), also when the camera
# then moves to the open sea. Fails on the view-centre rule (UI-WINDOW-1 R2/R4).
note fact hud.status.tile
hover_px 900 500
wait frames 5
expect fact hud.status.tile same
look 1000 320
wait frames 5
expect fact hud.status.tile same
expect fact hud.status.city == 1:1
expect fact hud.counters == materials+residents
expect fact hud.fertility == 6,8,11
# 3. Open sea: gold only, the row hidden at once.
hover-sea 1000 320
wait frames 5
expect fact hud.status.island == sea
expect fact hud.status.city == none
expect fact hud.counters == gold
expect fact hud.counters.city == none
expect fact hud.fertility == hidden
# 4. Another player's island (city 0:0 does not know player 1, nobody but player 0 discovered the
# island): gold only, no row.
look 692 142
wait frames 5
hover-land 692 142
wait frames 5
expect fact hud.status.island == 0
expect fact hud.status.city == 0:0
expect fact hud.counters == gold
expect fact hud.fertility == hidden
# 5. An undiscovered island without a city: gold only, no row.
look 928 232
wait frames 5
hover-sea 928 232
wait frames 5
expect fact hud.status.island == 10
expect fact hud.status.city == none
expect fact hud.counters == gold
expect fact hud.fertility == hidden
# 6. Sea inside the own island's rectangle (its north corner): the counters stay the city's (the
# developer start owns the whole rectangle); the row stays for 2 s of window time, then hides. The
# camera moves while the pointer is on the panel, so the row's delay starts only at the hover.
look 1140 516
wait frames 5
hover-land 1130 516
wait frames 5
expect fact hud.fertility == 6,8,11
hover_px 900 500
wait frames 2
look 1052 444
wait frames 5
expect fact hud.fertility == 6,8,11
expect fact hud.fertility.pending == no
hover-sea 1050 442
wait frames 1
expect fact hud.status.island == 1
expect fact hud.counters == materials+residents
expect fact hud.fertility.pending == yes
expect fact hud.fertility == 6,8,11
wait ms 2500
wait frames 3
expect fact hud.fertility == hidden
expect fact hud.fertility.pending == no
quit
